            <ArticleTitle>Stenting of coronary artery stenosis in Kawasaki disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>333-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery lesions can develop in Kawaski disease as a major complication, and result in aneurysm formation and stenosis. Reported is the evolution of important coronary artery stenosis in a pediatric patient managed with an endovascular stent.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
